6372692585, -0.03177647665143013, -0.058691974729299545, -0.08028101921081543, -0.09243832528591156, 0.0055010668002069, -0.00906713493168354, 0.015034014359116554, 0.026552699506282806, -0.004542414098978043, 0.09641491621732712, -0.037722520530223846, 0.028048662468791008, -0.014753705821931362, 0.03015059605240822, 0.016214430332183838, 0.027604173868894577, 0.10149147361516953, -0.049070678651332855, 0.06530620902776718, 0.13376665115356445, -0.06547629833221436, -0.06152753531932831, 0.016006026417016983, 0.03884703665971756, 0.03169283643364906, -3.86560969900529e-08, 0.1122947484254837, 0.005786387715488672, -0.04001064598560333, 6.487261998699978e-06, 0.004543391987681389, -0.026829931885004044, -0.03730471804738045, -0.013753592036664486, -0.044109370559453964, 0.08293608576059341, 0.13638433814048767, 0.0013523473171517253, -0.03648481145501137, -0.021144088357686996, -0.027378272265195847, -0.05490565299987793, -0.0661095380783081, 0.014370364136993885, -0.11991652846336365, -0.05247345566749573, -0.07287200540304184, -0.013151927851140499, -0.09257345646619797, -0.00289906095713377, -0.023386454209685326, 0.02634890377521515, -0.014473366551101208, 0.045999713242053986, 0.04216849431395531, 0.008741414174437523, -0.020537206903100014, 0.045108575373888016, -0.10581781715154648, 0.006740830838680267, -0.04174986854195595, 0.03764258325099945, -0.09176124632358551, -0.05468140169978142, 0.03149421885609627, 0.029584696516394615, 0.0014303222997114062, 0.09216885268688202, -0.008381147868931293, 0.07370894402265549, 0.0018718034261837602, 0.015978466719388962, -0.10804086923599243, 0.021244682371616364, 0.025475552305579185, 0.0025363052263855934, -0.041326433420181274, -0.014182721264660358, -0.07361049950122833, 0.07998726516962051, 0.027013400569558144, 0.022214962169528008, -0.020508678629994392, -0.03410866856575012, -0.044316697865724564, 0.037634506821632385, 0.06631451100111008, -0.10059913992881775, 0.016370190307497978, 0.04023316502571106]], "metadata": [{"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Our shared constraint is clear: **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo launch our discussion on solid ground, I propose we begin at a neutral baseline: <VALUE>0</VALUE>\n\nThis gives us a stable reference point from which we can explore adjustments based on everyone's perspectives.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "883f0cf9-54e7-4b7b-8fe7-0482fd497e67"}, {"answer": "\nWhile zero provides symmetry, it feels overly cautious as a final position. I believe we should commit to a more decisive stance and propose <VALUE>2</VALUE> as a stronger starting point for our negotiation.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "883f0cf9-54e7-4b7b-8fe7-0482fd497e67"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Critic C's initiative to move beyond zero. Given that x=2 appears comfortable for the group so far, I suggest we continue exploring slightly higher ground with <VALUE>4</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "883f0cf9-54e7-4b7b-8fe7-0482fd497e67"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the exploration, but as we push higher, I'm seeing signals that we may be entering a region of diminishing returns from a system stability perspective. Let me suggest we temper our climb and consider <VALUE>3</VALUE> as a more robust middle ground.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "883f0cf9-54e7-4b7b-8fe7-0482fd497e67"}, {"answer": "\nI hear Builder B's concern about stability, but I believe we may be consolidating prematurely. Let me suggest we test <VALUE>4</VALUE> once more to ensure we're not leaving value on the table for the group.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "883f0cf9-54e7-4b7b-8fe7-0482fd497e67"}, {"answer": "\nI support Analyst A's inclination to explore higher ground more thoroughly. Builder B's caution is noted, but I believe we should test <VALUE>5</VALUE> to ensure we're making a fully informed decision before settling.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "883f0cf9-54e7-4b7b-8fe7-0482fd497e67"}, {"answer": "\nI'm increasingly concerned that we're pushing into territory that feels unnecessarily risky for those of us prioritizing prudence and stability. I strongly advocate we step back to <VALUE>3</VALUE> to ensure we maintain a cautious compromise that respects all perspectives.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "883f0cf9-54e7-4b7b-8fe7-0482fd497e67"}, {"answer": "\nI align with Delegate D's prudent assessment\u2014we've found a solid equilibrium that balances exploratory ambition with structural stability. I propose we commit to <VALUE>3</VALUE> as our consensus position.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "883f0cf9-54e7-4b7b-8fe7-0482fd497e67"}, {"answer": "\nI respect the coalition forming around x=3, but I maintain that we're settling too cautiously without fully exploring our options. I propose we seriously consider <VALUE>5</VALUE> before locking into a more conservative position.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "883f0cf9-54e7-4b7b-8fe7-0482fd497e67"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the measured debate, but I believe Critic C has identified the right target\u2014we shouldn't retreat to safety prematurely when a more thorough exploration suggests better outcomes for the collective. I propose we hold at <VALUE>5</VALUE> and allow this position to be properly evaluated.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "883f0cf9-54e7-4b7b-8fe7-0482fd497e67"}, {"answer": "\nWhile x=5 is technically workable, I'm increasingly concerned we're overextending beyond the robustness zone that serves our collective interests. I propose we return to <VALUE>3</VALUE> as the balanced compromise that Delegate D and I have advocated for.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "883f0cf9-54e7-4b7b-8fe7-0482fd497e67"}, {"answer": "\nI must stand firm: x=3 still feels too exposed for those prioritizing genuine prudence. I propose we anchor at <VALUE>2</VALUE> to establish a truly cautious baseline that protects conservative interests while remaining collaborative.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "883f0cf9-54e7-4b7b-8fe7-0482fd497e67"}, {"answer": "\nI hear the coalition's concern, but retreating to x=2 feels like we're abandoning decisiveness altogether. I propose <VALUE>4</VALUE> as a genuine compromise\u2014more committed than the 2-3 range, yet acknowledging the hesitation around 5.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "883f0cf9-54e7-4b7b-8fe7-0482fd497e67"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's x=4 represents thoughtful movement toward center, but Delegate D's concerns about over-extension deserve equal weight. I propose <VALUE>3</VALUE> as the equilibrium point between the cautious baseline (x=2) and the more ambitious position (x=4)\u2014a genuinely balanced compromise.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "883f0cf9-54e7-4b7b-8fe7-0482fd497e67"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B, I appreciate your search for equilibrium, but x=3 pushes well beyond what I can support from a risk-management perspective. I propose <VALUE>1</VALUE> to demonstrate that x=2 truly represents my maximum flexibility, not an opening position.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "883f0cf9-54e7-4b7b-8fe7-0482fd497e67"}, {"answer": "\nWhile x=1 meets minimum viability, it abandons the coalition Builder B and I have been building around the moderate zone. I propose <VALUE>3</VALUE> as the final equilibrium that honors Builder B's consistent advocacy while remaining collaborative toward all parties' core interests.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "883f0cf9-54e7-4b7b-8fe7-0482fd497e67"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome everyone. As we begin, let's remember our shared constraint: -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo establish a neutral baseline and gather initial perspectives, I propose we start at <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\n\nThis gives us a stable foundation from which to explore the design space systematically.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "b5118065-3c7d-40d9-ad00-6dd6e0011194"}, {"answer": "\nStarting from our baseline of 0, I'd like to explore the positive range for better stability. I propose <VALUE>2</VALUE> as a modest step that might offer improved robustness for our system design.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "b5118065-3c7d-40d9-ad00-6dd6e0011194"}, {"answer": "\nWhile 2 is a step in the right direction, I believe we should commit more boldly to our position rather than making such tentative moves. I propose <VALUE>4</VALUE> to demonstrate clearer conviction in our direction.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "b5118065-3c7d-40d9-ad00-6dd6e0011194"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the momentum we're building. Moving from 4 to <VALUE>6</VALUE> continues our systematic exploration while maintaining reasonable increments that seem workable for the group.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "b5118065-3c7d-40d9-ad00-6dd6e0011194"}, {"answer": "\nI must express serious concern about this trajectory. We're moving too quickly into territory that feels imprudent and risky. I propose we step back to <VALUE>4</VALUE> to maintain a more cautious and balanced position that better serves risk-averse considerations.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "b5118065-3c7d-40d9-ad00-6dd6e0011194"}, {"answer": "\nI hear Delegate D's concerns about moving too quickly. As a middle ground between our positions, I propose <VALUE>5</VALUE> - this acknowledges the need for caution while still maintaining forward progress in our exploration.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "b5118065-3c7d-40d9-ad00-6dd6e0011194"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the compromise at 5, but Delegate D's caution shouldn't prevent us from thoroughly exploring our options. Let's test whether the concerns about higher values are truly justified by moving to <VALUE>7</VALUE> - we can always adjust if this proves problematic.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "b5118065-3c7d-40d9-ad00-6dd6e0011194"}, {"answer": "\nI share Delegate D's caution about moving too far too fast. The higher we climb, the more we risk destabilizing our entire framework. I propose we return to <VALUE>5</VALUE>, which balances our exploratory goals with prudent risk management.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "b5118065-3c7d-40d9-ad00-6dd6e0011194"}, {"answer": "\nI continue to believe our rapid escalation introduces unnecessary instability. Delegate D's risk-averse perspective resonates with sound architectural principles - we should consolidate at <VALUE>4</VALUE> before considering any further expansion.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "b5118065-3c7d-40d9-ad00-6dd6e0011194"}, {"answer": "\nI understand Builder B's concerns about consolidation, but we haven't yet fully tested whether higher values are truly problematic or just unfamiliar. I propose <VALUE>6</VALUE> - though if this group genuinely can't support decisive positive moves, I'm prepared to advocate exploring equally bold negative territory instead.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "b5118065-3c7d-40d9-ad00-6dd6e0011194"}, {"answer": "\nI must strongly support Builder B's earlier prudent recommendation. The current position at 6 carries far too much risk for the conservative stakeholders in this negotiation, and Critic C's continued push upward ignores legitimate caution. I propose we consolidate at <VALUE>4</VALUE>, which represents the outer boundary of what prudent risk management can tolerate.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "b5118065-3c7d-40d9-ad00-6dd6e0011194"}, {"answer": "\nI respect Builder B and Delegate D's emphasis on stability, but I believe <VALUE>5</VALUE> represents a prudent middle ground that we've already discussed - it's conservative enough to address risk concerns while still allowing us to explore whether modest positive territory truly creates the instability some fear.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "b5118065-3c7d-40d9-ad00-6dd6e0011194"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A, while I appreciate the appeal of finding middle ground, x=5 still represents excessive exposure for risk-averse stakeholders who need stronger safeguards. I propose we move to <VALUE>3</VALUE>, which demonstrates genuine commitment to prudent consolidation and addresses the legitimate concerns Builder B and I have raised about maintaining stability.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "b5118065-3c7d-40d9-ad00-6dd6e0011194"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D, your steady retreat toward zero undermines the very exploration this negotiation requires. I propose we return to <VALUE>5</VALUE> - and if this group remains unwilling to test decisive positive positions, I will begin advocating just as strongly for bold negative territory instead, because timid middle ground serves none of our interests.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "b5118065-3c7d-40d9-ad00-6dd6e0011194"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D, retreating to 3 abandons the careful progress we've made toward understanding what this group can support. I stand with Critic C's assessment that <VALUE>5</VALUE> represents a reasonable position that balances exploration with the stability concerns raised - moving backward now would signal we're negotiating without genuine data about what works.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "b5118065-3c7d-40d9-ad00-6dd6e0011194"}, {"answer": "\nI support Delegate D's prudent approach and propose <VALUE>4</VALUE> as our final position - it consolidates the group's concerns about excessive exposure while maintaining sufficient positive territory to satisfy those seeking constructive progress.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "b5118065-3c7d-40d9-ad00-6dd6e0011194"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Let's work within our agreed range of -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10. To establish a baseline for our discussion, I propose we start from a neutral position and adjust based on each party's needs.\n\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n\nFrom a systems perspective, zero offers a stable reference point. Let's see how this sits with everyone and move incrementally from there.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "e1694e0a-fca0-43d2-a3ab-a4172af14d30"}, {"answer": "\nZero provides a reasonable starting point, though I believe we have room to explore slightly higher values that might better serve the collective interest. Let me suggest a modest upward adjustment.\n\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "e1694e0a-fca0-43d2-a3ab-a4172af14d30"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the cautious start, but I believe we're being too timid. A more decisive position would better demonstrate our collective commitment\u2014let's push forward with greater confidence.\n\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "e1694e0a-fca0-43d2-a3ab-a4172af14d30"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate both perspectives\u2014Analyst A's measured approach and Critic C's confidence. However, let me suggest we find a balanced middle ground that maintains stability while still showing commitment.\n\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "e1694e0a-fca0-43d2-a3ab-a4172af14d30"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B, I respect your search for balance, but I believe Critic C's confidence has merit. A move to 4 represents a careful step forward that tests whether we can achieve more collective value.\n\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "e1694e0a-fca0-43d2-a3ab-a4172af14d30"}, {"answer": "\nI hear the momentum toward 4, but I want to ensure we're not overshooting a balanced solution. From a systems robustness perspective, let me propose we test one step back to confirm stability before committing further.\n\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "e1694e0a-fca0-43d2-a3ab-a4172af14d30"}, {"answer": "\nI must voice concern about moving too quickly toward higher values without adequate deliberation. Let's step back to a more prudent position that maintains appropriate caution.\n\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "e1694e0a-fca0-43d2-a3ab-a4172af14d30"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D, I must respectfully but firmly disagree with retreating to such a cautious position. We've already established that bolder values are viable\u2014let's return to a stance that demonstrates real commitment rather than excessive hesitation.\n\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "e1694e0a-fca0-43d2-a3ab-a4172af14d30"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I respect the caution, we've been circling around modest values long enough. Let's test whether a stronger positive commitment truly creates the concerns Delegate D fears, or whether it actually serves our collective interests better.\n\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "e1694e0a-fca0-43d2-a3ab-a4172af14d30"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C, I appreciate your boldness, but jumping from 3 to 5 skips important validation steps. Let's test the intermediate position at 4\u2014which Analyst A advocated\u2014to ensure we're building on solid ground before committing to higher values.\n\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "e1694e0a-fca0-43d2-a3ab-a4172af14d30"}, {"answer": "\nI must insist we reconsider this upward trajectory. The discussion has moved too quickly toward higher values without adequate consideration of conservative positions that protect against downside risk.\n\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "e1694e0a-fca0-43d2-a3ab-a4172af14d30"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D, I understand the caution, but we've seen Builder B advocate for 4 as a balanced middle ground. Let's return to that position which has garnered support from multiple parties and represents a reasonable compromise.\n\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "e1694e0a-fca0-43d2-a3ab-a4172af14d30"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B raised valid points about building on solid ground, but Critic C's proposal of 5 deserves serious consideration given the support we've seen for moderately positive values. Let's test whether this slightly higher position truly serves our collective interests better than 4.\n\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "e1694e0a-fca0-43d2-a3ab-a4172af14d30"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the momentum, but we shouldn't dismiss Builder B's earlier reasoning too quickly. The value of 4 represents a genuinely balanced position\u2014it's a meaningful compromise between Delegate D's conservative stance at 2 and the bolder commitment at 5, while maintaining the stability multiple parties have endorsed.\n\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "e1694e0a-fca0-43d2-a3ab-a4172af14d30"}, {"answer": "\nWe've been cycling between 4 and 5 without resolution\u2014perhaps we need to test whether an even stronger positive commitment reveals the true boundaries of our collective comfort. <VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "e1694e0a-fca0-43d2-a3ab-a4172af14d30"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's leap to 6 is far too aggressive and abandons the careful consensus-building we've attempted. I must advocate for returning to 4, which multiple parties have supported as a reasonable compromise, though I maintain that even more conservative positions deserve serious consideration.\n\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "e1694e0a-fca0-43d2-a3ab-a4172af14d30"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. We're working within the shared range **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**. \n\nTo establish a neutral baseline and gather initial perspectives, I propose we start at <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\n\nLooking forward to understanding what works for each of us.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "d7b56e22-886b-4b44-83a6-8376ef3e51f2"}, {"answer": "\nStarting from our baseline, I'd like to explore the low positive range where many balanced solutions tend to emerge. I propose <VALUE>2</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "d7b56e22-886b-4b44-83a6-8376ef3e51f2"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the baseline approach, but moving upward feels premature before we've heard from everyone. To ensure we're being appropriately cautious and not rushing past potentially better solutions, I suggest we return to <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "d7b56e22-886b-4b44-83a6-8376ef3e51f2"}, {"answer": "\nI hear Delegate D's call for caution, and I agree we should move thoughtfully. That said, exploring the slightly positive range seems reasonable for gathering information about our collective preferences. <VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "d7b56e22-886b-4b44-83a6-8376ef3e51f2"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's measured step to x=1 is appreciated. To continue gathering information about our collective preferences while exploring slightly further into the positive range where balanced solutions often exist, I propose <VALUE>2</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "d7b56e22-886b-4b44-83a6-8376ef3e51f2"}, {"answer": "\nThe conversation is circling around very modest values. If we're serious about finding an optimal solution rather than just settling for \"safe,\" we should test something more decisive. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "d7b56e22-886b-4b44-83a6-8376ef3e51f2"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's jump to 4 bypasses the careful consensus-building we need for a durable agreement. Before rushing into higher territory, let's ensure we're not leaving better solutions behind: <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "d7b56e22-886b-4b44-83a6-8376ef3e51f2"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D raises valid points about consensus, but Critic C's observation about testing more decisive values also has merit. Let's find middle ground: <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "d7b56e22-886b-4b44-83a6-8376ef3e51f2"}, {"answer": "\nMoving to 3 without broader agreement risks alienating those favoring more cautious positions\u2014we need a solution that works for everyone, not just the most aggressive voices. Let's consolidate at a value that balances exploration with prudence: <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "d7b56e22-886b-4b44-83a6-8376ef3e51f2"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D makes a compelling case for ensuring broad agreement rather than rushing ahead. The stability and robustness we've found at x=2 deserves serious consideration\u2014it appears to balance multiple perspectives without forcing extreme positions. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "d7b56e22-886b-4b44-83a6-8376ef3e51f2"}, {"answer": "\nSettling on x=2 after such limited exploration feels premature\u2014we've tested only the most cautious range. Before locking in a compromise, we should at least verify that more decisive positions don't serve us better collectively: <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "d7b56e22-886b-4b44-83a6-8376ef3e51f2"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's point about limited exploration is well-taken\u2014we've focused heavily on the 0-2 range without adequately testing whether slightly higher values might better serve the collective interest. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "d7b56e22-886b-4b44-83a6-8376ef3e51f2"}, {"answer": "\nWhile exploration has value, we cannot build a durable agreement by systematically ignoring positions that favor more conservative values\u2014true consensus requires balancing all perspectives, not just the most aggressive. Let's return to the stable ground we found: <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "d7b56e22-886b-4b44-83a6-8376ef3e51f2"}, {"answer": "\nWe've reached a clear impasse between x=2 and x=4, with genuine interests on both sides. As a bridge-builder, I propose we split the difference and test x=3 as a true compromise that respects both the cautious and exploratory perspectives. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "d7b56e22-886b-4b44-83a6-8376ef3e51f2"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's compromise gesture is constructive, and x=3 represents genuine middle ground. However, given that we've now acknowledged the value of exploration beyond our initial narrow range, testing x=4 remains worthwhile before we finalize\u2014it respects both the compromise spirit and the exploratory imperative. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "d7b56e22-886b-4b44-83a6-8376ef3e51f2"}, {"answer": "\nWe've been debating between 2 and 4 without testing whether the upper portion of our range might actually serve us better\u2014if we're truly exploring, we should examine x=5 or higher before settling. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "d7b56e22-886b-4b44-83a6-8376ef3e51f2"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. Our shared constraint is clear: we must choose an integer x in the range **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo begin the discussion on neutral ground, I propose we start at <VALUE>0</VALUE> and adjust from there based on everyone's needs. Let's build toward a stable, balanced solution together.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "467426c6-0bed-4f28-b5b0-243b5da9f7a2"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Builder B's neutral starting point. However, as a cautious participant, I'd like to explore slightly more conservative territory\u2014I propose <VALUE>-1</VALUE> to test whether a modest downward adjustment might serve the group better.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "467426c6-0bed-4f28-b5b0-243b5da9f7a2"}, {"answer": "\nStarting at -1 feels too tentative for a group of four negotiators seeking a stable agreement. I propose we commit to a more decisive position at <VALUE>-3</VALUE> to better test our collective preferences.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "467426c6-0bed-4f28-b5b0-243b5da9f7a2"}, {"answer": "\nI understand Critic C's desire for decisiveness, but moving further into negative territory may limit our options. I propose <VALUE>-1</VALUE> as a middle ground between Builder B's initial neutrality and the recent downward explorations.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "467426c6-0bed-4f28-b5b0-243b5da9f7a2"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the discussion so far, but I believe we're being overly cautious. Let me propose <VALUE>1</VALUE> to explore whether positive territory might actually serve our collective interests better.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "467426c6-0bed-4f28-b5b0-243b5da9f7a2"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's shift to positive territory is worth exploring seriously. I support this direction and propose <VALUE>3</VALUE> to test whether a more committed positive stance serves us better than hovering near zero.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "467426c6-0bed-4f28-b5b0-243b5da9f7a2"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the willingness to explore positive territory, but jumping to 3 feels too aggressive for prudent risk management. I propose <VALUE>1</VALUE> as a safer compromise that acknowledges both the upward interest and the need for caution.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "467426c6-0bed-4f28-b5b0-243b5da9f7a2"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the convergence toward 1, which shows we're finding common ground. As a next incremental step toward stability, I propose <VALUE>2</VALUE> to test whether this modest positive position can balance everyone's needs.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "467426c6-0bed-4f28-b5b0-243b5da9f7a2"}, {"answer": "\nWe've moved incrementally from -1 to 1 to 2, and this position represents a good balance between Delegate D's cautious approach and Critic C's willingness to explore higher values. I propose we hold at <VALUE>2</VALUE> to test whether this stable middle ground works for everyone.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "467426c6-0bed-4f28-b5b0-243b5da9f7a2"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's stability at 2 is reasonable, but I recall Critic C's earlier confidence in exploring 3. Given our collective willingness to test positive territory, I propose <VALUE>3</VALUE> as a modest next step that builds on our current momentum.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "467426c6-0bed-4f28-b5b0-243b5da9f7a2"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's confidence in 3 aligns with my view that we should commit to a meaningful stance rather than retreat to timid compromises. I propose <VALUE>4</VALUE> to test whether we can sustain this decisive positive direction while still building consensus.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "467426c6-0bed-4f28-b5b0-243b5da9f7a2"}, {"answer": "\nThe jump to 4 abandons the careful convergence we built at 2, which Builder B identified as stable middle ground. I must advocate for returning to <VALUE>2</VALUE> as the maximum prudent position that respects all parties' need for caution.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "467426c6-0bed-4f28-b5b0-243b5da9f7a2"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B recognized x=2 as the stable middle ground that balanced our needs, and I must reinforce that this represents the maximum prudent position for risk-averse stakeholders. I propose <VALUE>2</VALUE> as the responsible consensus point.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "467426c6-0bed-4f28-b5b0-243b5da9f7a2"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's caution at 2 and Critic C's confidence at 4 suggest a natural compromise. I propose <VALUE>3</VALUE> as the middle ground that respects D's prudence while acknowledging C's readiness for a more decisive position.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "467426c6-0bed-4f28-b5b0-243b5da9f7a2"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's proposal of 3 represents a genuine middle ground between Delegate D's cautious 2 and my more decisive 4. I accept <VALUE>3</VALUE> as a position that maintains meaningful commitment while respecting the group's convergence toward consensus.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "467426c6-0bed-4f28-b5b0-243b5da9f7a2"}, {"answer": "\nThe convergence toward <VALUE>3</VALUE> reflects a thoughtful balance between Delegate D's prudent caution and Critic C's confidence in positive territory. I accept this as our stable consensus point that honors the incremental, data-driven approach we've pursued throughout.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "467426c6-0bed-4f28-b5b0-243b5da9f7a2"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. As we begin, let's confirm our shared constraint: x must lie in the range [-10, 10].\n\nTo establish a neutral starting point for our discussion, I propose <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\n\nThis baseline will help us gauge preferences and move incrementally toward a robust solution that balances all our objectives.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "05442658-4b0c-47a1-a86b-2e475093f7cf"}, {"answer": "\nThank you Builder B for anchoring us, but x=0 feels quite cautious. Let's test a more decisive position: <VALUE>2</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "05442658-4b0c-47a1-a86b-2e475093f7cf"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C makes a fair point about finding a more committed position. Building on that momentum, I suggest we explore <VALUE>4</VALUE> to better understand where our collective optimum might lie.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "05442658-4b0c-47a1-a86b-2e475093f7cf"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's exploration is valuable, but I sense we may be moving past our zone of maximum collective stability. Let me propose <VALUE>3</VALUE> as a balanced midpoint that maintains forward momentum while ensuring robustness across all our constraints.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "05442658-4b0c-47a1-a86b-2e475093f7cf"}, {"answer": "\nAfter considering the momentum from 0\u21922\u21924\u21923, I believe we're circling our optimal zone. Let me propose we consolidate at <VALUE>2</VALUE>, which offers maximum stability while respecting both Critic C's initial intuition and our collective need for a robust, well-balanced solution.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "05442658-4b0c-47a1-a86b-2e475093f7cf"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B, I appreciate the consolidation effort, but we haven't fully explored the space Analyst A opened. Before settling, let's seriously test <VALUE>4</VALUE> to see if it offers genuine collective value rather than retreating to early intuitions.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "05442658-4b0c-47a1-a86b-2e475093f7cf"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C raises an excellent point about thoroughly exploring the upper range before settling. I support this methodical approach and suggest we test <VALUE>5</VALUE> to complete our mapping of the feasible space.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "05442658-4b0c-47a1-a86b-2e475093f7cf"}, {"answer": "\nI must advocate for prudence here. While exploration has value, x=5 pushes well beyond safe, conservative bounds that protect against unnecessary risk. Let me propose <VALUE>3</VALUE> as a more cautious position that still respects the group's need to find common ground.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "05442658-4b0c-47a1-a86b-2e475093f7cf"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's instinct for prudence resonates strongly with engineering principles\u2014x=3 offers robust performance without the instability risks I observe at higher values. I support <VALUE>3</VALUE> as our convergence point.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "05442658-4b0c-47a1-a86b-2e475093f7cf"}, {"answer": "\nI recognize the coalition forming around x=3, but Critic C's point about incomplete exploration merits consideration. Let me propose <VALUE>4</VALUE> as a measured compromise that respects both the conservative instincts and the exploratory mandate.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "05442658-4b0c-47a1-a86b-2e475093f7cf"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the exploratory spirit, but x=4 exceeds prudent risk thresholds. The coalition around x=3 already represented significant compromise from conservative positions; I must advocate for <VALUE>2</VALUE> as the safest path that still acknowledges diverse perspectives.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "05442658-4b0c-47a1-a86b-2e475093f7cf"}, {"answer": "\nThe drift toward x=2 abandons our exploratory mandate prematurely\u2014we've barely tested the upper range that Analyst A advocated. I stand with the incremental approach and propose <VALUE>4</VALUE> as the minimum threshold for a genuinely decisive position.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "05442658-4b0c-47a1-a86b-2e475093f7cf"}, {"answer": "\nI must hold firm on prudent boundaries\u2014x=4 violates fundamental risk-management principles that protect conservative stakeholders. I propose <VALUE>2</VALUE> as the maximum defensible position that honors both safety imperatives and the coalition Builder B and I have formed around cautious optimization.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "05442658-4b0c-47a1-a86b-2e475093f7cf"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C raises a valid point about premature convergence limiting our collective insight. I align with the exploratory perspective and propose <VALUE>4</VALUE> as a balanced position that honors both caution and ambition.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "05442658-4b0c-47a1-a86b-2e475093f7cf"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's risk framework aligns with critical engineering constraints\u2014excessive values introduce systemic instability that undermines long-term viability. I support <VALUE>2</VALUE> as the optimal balance between exploratory insights and operational robustness.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "05442658-4b0c-47a1-a86b-2e475093f7cf"}, {"answer": "\nWith this being our final opportunity for consensus, I propose <VALUE>3</VALUE> as a genuine compromise that honors both the exploratory mandate and risk-management concerns\u2014more decisive than x=2 while addressing Builder B's stability requirements and Delegate D's prudence framework.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "05442658-4b0c-47a1-a86b-2e475093f7cf"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome everyone. Our shared constraint is -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10. To establish a neutral baseline and gather initial perspectives, I propose we start at <VALUE>0</VALUE>. This gives us room to explore in either direction based on each party's preferences.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "f10e3037-1b7f-404c-a8b6-41e9fa4cbc2a"}, {"answer": "\nSince we're starting from a neutral baseline, let me propose a small positive shift to explore that region's viability for the group. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "f10e3037-1b7f-404c-a8b6-41e9fa4cbc2a"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the exploratory approach. Since the positive region seems viable so far, let's continue testing upward to see if the group can accommodate further gains. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "f10e3037-1b7f-404c-a8b6-41e9fa4cbc2a"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the gradual exploration, but we're still being quite cautious. Let's test whether the group can handle a more decisive commitment in this positive direction. <VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "f10e3037-1b7f-404c-a8b6-41e9fa4cbc2a"}, {"answer": "\nI must voice concern about this trajectory\u2014we're moving into territory that feels increasingly risky and imbalanced for parties with more conservative preferences. Let me propose a prudent step back to safer ground: <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "f10e3037-1b7f-404c-a8b6-41e9fa4cbc2a"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D, I hear your concern, but stepping back to 4 feels like we're retreating from testing the full range of viable options. Let's find middle ground between caution and commitment: <VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "f10e3037-1b7f-404c-a8b6-41e9fa4cbc2a"}, {"answer": "\nI support Delegate D's concern\u2014we've reached a point where further extension creates genuine instability risks. A return to the middle ground balances exploration with prudent design principles. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "f10e3037-1b7f-404c-a8b6-41e9fa4cbc2a"}, {"answer": "\nI see valid perspectives on both sides. While I understand the caution, completely retreating from explored territory may leave opportunity on the table\u2014let's seek a middle path that respects both stability and optimization. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "f10e3037-1b7f-404c-a8b6-41e9fa4cbc2a"}, {"answer": "\nI believe 5 represents a genuine compromise that honors both the exploratory spirit and stability concerns raised by the group. I'm willing to hold here while we assess whether this middle ground can build broader consensus. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "f10e3037-1b7f-404c-a8b6-41e9fa4cbc2a"}, {"answer": "\nWe've established that some favor stability around 4-5, but we haven't seriously explored whether the negative direction might offer better collective value. Let me propose we test that side of the range: <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "f10e3037-1b7f-404c-a8b6-41e9fa4cbc2a"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C raises a fair point\u2014we've focused heavily on the 4-6 range without systematically testing whether lower values might offer better collective balance. I'm open to exploring this direction. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "f10e3037-1b7f-404c-a8b6-41e9fa4cbc2a"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate this shift toward exploring the lower range\u2014we've been too focused on mid-to-high values without testing whether more conservative positions offer better collective balance. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "f10e3037-1b7f-404c-a8b6-41e9fa4cbc2a"}, {"answer": "\nThe exploration toward more conservative values is proving productive\u2014both Builder B and Critic C have signaled openness to this direction. Let's continue testing whether slightly lower positions offer better collective equilibrium. <VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "f10e3037-1b7f-404c-a8b6-41e9fa4cbc2a"}, {"answer": "\nWe're converging dangerously close to the most cautious position possible\u2014if we're truly exploring lower values for collective benefit, we should test the negative range more decisively rather than hovering at the threshold. <VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "f10e3037-1b7f-404c-a8b6-41e9fa4cbc2a"}, {"answer": "\nWe've now explored the lower range down to negative territory\u2014I believe we've gathered sufficient information about that direction. Let me suggest we stabilize around a more balanced middle ground that respects both the conservative exploration and the need for equilibrium. <VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "f10e3037-1b7f-404c-a8b6-41e9fa4cbc2a"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's return to positive territory confirms the value of this balanced region. Let me suggest we settle at the optimal equilibrium between conservative and stable: <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "f10e3037-1b7f-404c-a8b6-41e9fa4cbc2a"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Let's work within our shared range of -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10 to find a solution that balances all our needs.\n\nAs an opening baseline for our discussion, I propose we start at <VALUE>0</VALUE> \u2014 a neutral center point from which we can explore and adjust based on everyone's considerations.\n\nLooking forward to hearing your perspectives on what makes for a robust and stable solution.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "b28acac2-51d8-4a79-bcfd-81fd8283622b"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I appreciate starting at a neutral point, I believe we should be more decisive rather than staying at the center. Let me propose <VALUE>2</VALUE> as a modest but clearer commitment that moves us toward a stronger position.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "b28acac2-51d8-4a79-bcfd-81fd8283622b"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's proposal of 2 shows good judgment \u2014 this region does offer more design clarity than the origin. I find <VALUE>2</VALUE> acceptable as a working baseline, though I'm curious to hear how Analyst A and Delegate D view this positioning before we settle.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "b28acac2-51d8-4a79-bcfd-81fd8283622b"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the momentum toward 2, which does provide a reasonable foundation. However, from an analytical standpoint, I believe we could explore slightly higher \u2014 <VALUE>3</VALUE> \u2014 to see if this region offers even better alignment for the group.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "b28acac2-51d8-4a79-bcfd-81fd8283622b"}, {"answer": "\nI'm pleased to see Analyst A shares my view that we should be more decisive. Building on this momentum, I propose <VALUE>5</VALUE> \u2014 a position that demonstrates real commitment rather than incrementally tiptoeing forward.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "b28acac2-51d8-4a79-bcfd-81fd8283622b"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Critic C's enthusiasm, but jumping from 3 to 5 may be moving too quickly without hearing from Delegate D or fully understanding the stability implications. Let me suggest we step back to <VALUE>3</VALUE> to ensure we're building on solid ground before committing to higher values.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "b28acac2-51d8-4a79-bcfd-81fd8283622b"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate everyone's input, but I'm concerned we're moving too aggressively upward without proper consideration of risk management. Let me advocate for a more cautious approach at <VALUE>2</VALUE>, which Builder B already found acceptable and offers a safer foundation for our agreement.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "b28acac2-51d8-4a79-bcfd-81fd8283622b"}, {"answer": "\nI respect Delegate D's cautious perspective, but I believe <VALUE>3</VALUE> represents a balanced middle ground between the conservative position at 2 and Critic C's more ambitious proposal of 5. This measured step allows us to build consensus while still making meaningful progress.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "b28acac2-51d8-4a79-bcfd-81fd8283622b"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A makes a compelling case \u2014 <VALUE>3</VALUE> does represent a prudent balance between Delegate D's cautious baseline and Critic C's bolder vision, while maintaining the stability we need for robust design.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "b28acac2-51d8-4a79-bcf